      "question": {
        ":question/id": "99e025e4-1ea6-5d6e-812a-92d3fa45174a",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4{y}^{3}}{{(12-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=12-{y}^{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=-4{y}^{3}\\,\u27f9\\,(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{d}u={y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{y}^{3}}{{(12-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{(12-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{(12-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
